---
import Service from '../layouts/Service.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Does composite decking get hot in Utah summers?', a: 'All decking gets warm in direct sun, and darker colors get hotter. Lighter colors, capped PVC lines and a pergola or shade sail make a big difference on west-facing decks.' },
  { q: 'Which is better, Trex or TimberTech?', a: 'Both are excellent. Trex offers great value and a wide color range. TimberTech AZEK PVC boards run cooler and lighter and carry longer warranties at a higher price. We bring samples so you can compare in person.' },
  { q: 'How long does a composite deck last?', a: 'Most composite decking carries a 25 to 50 year manufacturer warranty against fading and staining, depending on the line. The framing underneath is what usually determines how long a deck lasts, which is why we protect it.' },
  { q: 'Do composite decks need maintenance?', a: 'No sanding, staining or sealing. Wash it with soap and water or a low-pressure rinse a couple times a year and clear snow with a plastic shovel.' },
];
---
<Service
  slug="composite-decks"
  name="Composite Decks"
  title="Composite Deck Installation in Utah County | TC Decks"
  description="TimberTech PVC and composite deck installation in Saratoga Springs, Lehi and Utah County. Compare brands, colors and warranties. Free estimate."
  h1="Composite deck installation"
  lead="Composite decking holds up to Utah's sun, snow and freeze-thaw cycles without staining or sealing. We install the major brands and help you choose the right line for your budget."
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <h2>Composite vs. wood in Utah</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th></th><th>Pressure-treated wood</th><th>Composite / PVC</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Upfront cost</td><td>Lower</td><td>Higher</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Maintenance</td><td>Stain/seal every 2–3 years</td><td>Wash occasionally</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Splinters, cracking</td><td>Common as it ages</td><td>No</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Fade &amp; stain warranty</td><td>None</td><td>25–50 years</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Long-term cost</td><td>Rises with upkeep</td><td>Often lower over 10+ years</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Why we recommend TimberTech</h2>
  <p>For most decks we recommend TimberTech. Its fully capped PVC boards absorb almost no water, stay cooler underfoot than traditional composite, and resist fading and staining in Utah's high-altitude sun. The lines are grouped good, better and best:</p>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li><strong>Good:</strong> Prime+, Premier, Terrain, Terrain+</li>
    <li><strong>Better:</strong> Harvest, Harvest+, Landmark, Reserve</li>
    <li><strong>Best:</strong> Legacy, Vintage</li>
  </ul>
  <p>See every line, plus colors and design details, in our <a href="/design-ideas/composite-decking">decking &amp; colors guide</a>.</p>
  <h3>Other brands</h3>
  <p>As a <a href="/certified-pro-installer">certified Pro Installer</a> for TimberTech, Trex and Deckorators, we can offer manufacturer-backed labor and material warranty coverage. We also install Fiberon. We've built many Trex decks over the years, including Transcend in Lava Rock, Spiced Rum and Havana Gold, and we're happy to match an existing deck or a brand you already love.</p>

  <Photo src="/images/ideas/two-tone-deck-border-railing" alt="Two-tone composite decking with a contrasting border" />

  <h2>Railings, lighting and finishing touches</h2>
  <p>We pair your decking with Fortress aluminum, glass, cable or composite railing, picture-frame borders, hidden fasteners and low-voltage lighting so the whole deck looks like one design.</p>
  <p>Wondering what your deck will cost? <a href="/contact">Get a free estimate</a>.</p>
</Service>
